the world is an unpredictable place  that's what makes it so haunting when  you watch a movie years after it's come  out and you realize that the filmmakers  unintentionally predicted real-world  tragedies you'll never be able to watch  these movies the same way again  Game of Death Game of Death was released  in 1978 five years after its lead actor  Bruce Lee had died but the completed  movie which was rewritten after Lee died  of unrelated medical complications  during the production contains a truly  eerie plot point Lee plays Billy Lowe an  actor who shot with a prop gun that  turns out to have a real bullet in it  the shot isn't fatal but Lowe fakes his  death to take revenge on the would-be  assassins in 1993 Bruce Lee's son  Brandon Lee died while filming The Crow  an actor was supposed to fire an  unloaded gun at Brandon but a bullet  fragment that was previously stuck in  the barrel dislodged while shooting the  blank cartridge it struck Brandon with  the same velocity as a real round  Brandon Lee died under nearly the same  circumstances depicted in his father's  final movie demolition men demolition  man from 1993 predicted a high-profile  murder nearly a decade before it  happened the sci-fi film involved a  cryoprison where criminals are frozen  and put in cold storage at one point in  the movie the prisoners who are frozen  with Stallone's character and the  criminal he caught appear on a jailhouse  monitor one of the names that pops up is  Scott Peterson a name probably chosen by  an intern or low-level production  assistant fewer than 10 years later in  2002 a woman named Lacey Peterson was  brutally murdered by her husband Scott  Peterson he was convicted of killing  Lacey and their unborn son in 2004 and  was sentenced to death a year later in  the years after his conviction and  sentencing he was a death row inmate in  California's San Quentin prison  meanwhile the cryoprison and demolition  man was where California kept their  worst prisoners their death row inmates  the matrix to say the prop designer on  the set of the matrix from 1999 may have  inadvertently predicted the worst act of  terror inflicted on the United States of  America is both unnerving and more  importantly not meant to show disrespect  to any of the Fallen however when  watching the movie now it's difficult to  ignore the expiration date on Thomas neo  Anderson's passport which is 9 1101  poltergeist poltergeist is spooky enough  but it doesn't end there the children's  room includes a fake Super Bowl 22  poster which would be happening in 1988  six years after the movie debuted in  theaters weirdly enough that poster  inadvertently predicted when Heather  O'Rourke the child star who's abducted  by ghosts in the movie would become  fatally sick as Super Bowl 22 came  around on January 31st 1988 O'Rourke  fell violently ill before passing away  the next day due to a cardiac arrest  triggered by an intestinal stenosis  World's Greatest Dad  in 2009 World's Greatest Dad Robin  Williams plays Lance Clayton a dad and  English teacher whose teenage son  accidentally dies from autoerotic  asphyxiation Clayton not wanting the  police or anyone else to find his son's  body like that makes it look like a  suicide instead Williams's portrayal of  Clayton combined with his heartfelt  characters who dealt with suicide and  what dreams may come  patch Adams and Dead Poets Society makes  his tragic suicide in 2014 stand out  even more thanks for watching subscribe  to our YouTube channel to watch more  videos like the one you just saw
 

